# Landing + Demo server-side env template — /etc/juli/frontend.env
#
# Source of truth is the AWS Secrets Manager secret `juli/frontend/production`;
# fetch-secrets.sh writes this file from it, refresh-secrets.sh keeps it in
# sync and restarts whichever Landing/Demo unit is actually live. NEVER commit
# real values.
#
# WHY A SEPARATE FILE from landing-runtime.env / demo-runtime.env: those two
# are written by the deploy scripts on every release (write_runtime_env,
# write_demo_runtime_env) and they TRUNCATE. A secret placed in either would
# survive exactly until the next deploy.
#
# NOT a NEXT_PUBLIC_* value, and it must never become one — Next inlines those
# into the browser bundle at build time, which would publish the token.
#
# The secret is OPTIONAL to the deploy: fetch-secrets.sh warns and continues if
# it does not exist, so a missing token can never stop a release. The relay
# route answers 503 and logs once a minute instead.

# TikTok Events API access token for data source DAO9C6JC77U88MSNU74G.
# Generate: Events Manager -> the data source -> Settings -> Events API ->
# "Generate access token". It authorises writes to this one data source only.
TIKTOK_EVENTS_API_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# Optional. Set to a code from Events Manager -> Test Events to route events to
# the Test Events tab instead of reporting, for verifying a deploy without
# polluting live conversions. MUST be unset in production.
# TIKTOK_EVENTS_API_TEST_EVENT_CODE=
